From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:36:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] fix(qti): use a PMIC hard reset for SYSTEM_RESET

PSCI SYSTEM_RESET is a cold reset (a warm one is SYSTEM_RESET2), but
qti_pmic_prepare_reset() programs a PMIC warm reset for it. The Lemans
EVK (IQ-9075) never comes back from that: nothing boots until a power
cycle.

Program the hard reset instead, for every platform.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Change-Id: I77732b967259be8a2d9e8a110e69e610eabea537
Link: https://review.trustedfirmware.org/c/55766
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/trusted-firmware-a/commit/a467848d31c3dccd7a3100deed11da39ef3a474f]
Signed-off-by: Roshan Sivakumar <roshs@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 plat/qti/common/src/pm_ps_hold.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/qti/common/src/pm_ps_hold.c b/plat/qti/common/src/pm_ps_hold.c
index 208345cc1..b3f8040a6 100644
--- a/plat/qti/common/src/pm_ps_hold.c
+++ b/plat/qti/common/src/pm_ps_hold.c
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
  * include other part numbers like PM6150.
  */
 
-#define RESET_TYPE_WARM_RESET		1
+#define RESET_TYPE_HARD_RESET		7
 #define RESET_TYPE_SHUTDOWN		4
 
 #define S2_RESET_EN			BIT(7)
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ static void configure_ps_hold(uint32_t reset_type)
 
 void qti_pmic_prepare_reset(void)
 {
-	configure_ps_hold(RESET_TYPE_WARM_RESET);
+	configure_ps_hold(RESET_TYPE_HARD_RESET);
 }
 
 void qti_pmic_prepare_shutdown(void)
